    rdfs:label "variance_explained" ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/STATO_0000564> ;
    skos:definition "Proportion of variance accounted for, e.g. R2, adjusted R2, or an ordination axis's share of the explained variance." ;
    warp:note "close, not exact: an ordination axis's share of variance is not a coefficient of determination." ;
    warp:preferred_label "coefficient of determination" .

<https://w3id.org/ecoweaver/warp/EntityTypeEnum#taxon> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        warp:EntityTypeEnum ;
    rdfs:label "taxon" ;
    skos:definition """A taxon that is the subject of a causal claim. Refers to all members of that taxon, with the caveats specified in causal annotation layers.\r
Two-path model for taxon-specific measurements:\r
(1) Single-taxon measurement — use entity_type: taxon with the NCBITaxon ID in entity_term and the measured property in measured_attribute. The node is both the organism and the measurement (e.g., entity_term=NCBITaxon:9612, measured_attribute=cover, qualifier=increased gives "increased Sphagnum cover"). The taxon node participates directly in causal edges.\r
(2) Multi-taxon aggregate or ecological guild — use entity_type: composite_variable with applied_to listing the relevant NCBITaxon IDs or free-text guild names. Reserve this for cases where the measurement spans multiple taxa ("richness of liverworts, Sphagnum, and true mosses") or refers to an ecologically defined group with no single NCBITaxon resolution ("native species", "shade-tolerant species"). Edges remain purely causal; applied_to is a queryable annotation field, not a structural link.""" .

